WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.360
Add waist shaping to any sweater
with a little math and the

00:00:05.426 --> 00:00:08.240
Knit It Now Magic formula tools.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.410
This summer sweater has no waist shaping.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.410
A fellow knitter, Sandy,
decided she wanted to shape her sweater

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.730
by removing a total of eight inches,
four inches from the front

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.970
and four inches from the back.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.080
We'll create shaping
instructions in two steps.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:33.210
First, after the one-inch hem, we'll start
to decrease for five inches to the waist.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:40.000
For a better fit and drape, we'll knit
one inch without any shaping at the waist.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.650
Then we'll immediately increase for five
inches back up to the bust width.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.810
The goal is to decrease gradually from hip
to waist and then increase back

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.960
waist to bust.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.090
We'll use the Knit It Now
Magic Formula tool for this.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.520
Go to Patterns, Charting Tools.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.200
Since we know our dimensions,
we'll use the Magic Formula

00:01:08.266 --> 00:01:11.240
tool in inches or centimeters.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:19.080
We will be shaping both sides
of the piece, her gage at 28 and 38.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:28.250
The starting width at the hem is 18 inches
and the waist is going to be 14 inches.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.920
The height of this section is 5 inches.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.890
Now be sure to let the tool know if
you're working in inches or centimeters.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.930
And click Create your
Knitting Instructions.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.570
Here are her knitting instructions.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.410
Draw her on and out,
you can see that there's a nice

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.920
smooth line for her sweater.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.530
We'll do the same thing for the upper
part of this waist shaping.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:02:01.600
Again, using the tool for both sides,
I'll enter her gage, then the starting

00:02:01.666 --> 00:02:04.800
and ending width and height.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:12.970
She will insert these instructions
when knitting the body of her sweater.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.410
With the tool, there's
no complicated math.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.094
Just determine the measurements you want
and create your custom

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:19.720
knitting instructions.

